# Vendored third-party source: the MuseTalk checkout the renderer imports. Upstream publishes no
# distribution and its modules import each other by top-level name, so the tree has to be on
# sys.path -- but it is someone else's source under its own licence, and committing it would put
# an unmaintained fork in this repo. `scripts/setup_musetalk.sh` clones it.
vendor/

# Prepared idle-loop frames (regenerate with scripts/prepare_idle_loop.py)
assets/idle_frames/

# Measurement artifacts
measurements/*.json

# Secrets. No exemption, deliberately: a committed template is one `git add -f` away from
# a committed key, and README's Configuration table documents every variable instead.
.env
.env.*

# Local working files. Not deliverables, and kept out of the published repo: an
# assistant-configuration file and a personal work log are not what a reader of this
# repository is here for, and a checked-in permission bypass would apply to everyone
# who clones it.
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
DEVLOG.md
NOTES.local.md

# Working notes kept out of the published repo: a spike runbook, a manual test protocol,
# and cloud-GPU setup steps. Their conclusions live in PROCESS.md, which is the deliverable;
# the runbooks themselves are process material and read as such.
docs/

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
node_modules

# Node / Next.js
node_modules/
.next/
out/
.turbo/
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Runtime store. One JSON file per agent, rubric, session and knowledge base, written by
# `avatar.store`. Untracked because it is state, not source -- but the reason it is *ignored*
# rather than merely untracked is that session records hold interview transcripts: what a
# candidate said, verbatim. One `git add -A` from a demo run would publish them.
#
# Unanchored on purpose. `AVATAR_DATA_DIR` defaults to a *relative* "data", so the store lands
# wherever the process was started from -- and a uvicorn launched from the repo root put a real
# session transcript in /data, which the anchored `apps/api/data/` rule did not cover and which
# duly got committed. Matching the directory at any depth is the only version that holds.
data/

# Archived copies of the file store, taken when migrating to Postgres. Same contents as `data/`
# — verbatim interview transcripts — so the same rule applies, and a tarball is easier to
# accidentally commit than a directory.
data-archive-*.tar.gz

# Finished recordings, bind-mounted out of the egress container. Interviews, in video form -- the
# same reason `data/` is ignored, only larger and harder to un-publish.
recordings/

# Uploaded reference media: a real person's face and voice, provided for a persona. Same class of
# content as `recordings/` and ignored for the same reason.
media/

# Generated decks. scripts/make_deck.py rebuilds them; the numbers live in that script.
*.pptx

# Seeded resumes are generated by scripts/seed_demo.py; they are invented people, but a
# repository is the wrong place for anything shaped like a personal document.
apps/api/data/
